<!--META-DATA
{
	tags: for, sum,
}
-->

<statement>
<p>
	This program implements the game loop for a player-versus-player (PVP) version of Tic-Tac-Toe.
</p>

<tabular valign="top" top="minor">
	<col width="12%"/>
	<col width="88%"/>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Inputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>state</pf> (1 x 1) number — struct object containing the initial state of a PVP Tic-Tac-Toe game.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell>Outputs:</cell>
		<cell>
			<p><pf>state</pf> (1 x 1) number — struct object containing the final state of a PVP Tic-Tac-Toe game.</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell>Details:</cell>
		<cell><p>Assume the first player is the X player.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>The game loop should repeat at most nine rounds of a Tic-Tac-Toe game.</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>Each round should consist of the following tasks:</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell>
			<p>
				<ul>
					<li>Get a valid click from a single player,</li>
					<li>Update the game_state structure,</li>
					<li>Update the game interface,</li>
					<li>Check for a winner.</li>
				</ul>
			</p>
		</cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>This program should return an updated</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row>
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>game_state</p></cell>
	</row>
	<row bottom="minor">
		<cell/>
		<cell><p>structure containing the game's results.</p></cell>
	</row>
</tabular>

</statement>
